  "description": "This retrospective planning application is submitted to formalize the current arrangement at\n49 Cranbury Road. This application is prompted by a caveat raised by Ms. Tembo in previous\npermissions and/or the Certificate of Lawful Development.\nIt is important to clarify that this application is not retrospective in the sense of seeking\npermission for entirely new works. Instead, it serves to consolidate and confirm an\narrangement that is substantially similar to, and effectively a combination of, elements\npreviously granted approval under separate permissions.\nSpecifically, this application concerns:\n\nThe addition of a glass balustrade (approved in application 2025/00159/NMAT) to the\ntop of a rear extension (approved in application 2025/00133/CLP).\nThis combined arrangement creates a platform that is very similar to the arrangement\nagreed in application reference 2024/02428/FUL.\nWe believe that, when viewed collectively, the previous approvals already provide the\nnecessary consent for the arrangement as it currently exists. This application therefore seeks\nto bring all relevant permissions together under a single reference, addressing Ms. Tembo's\ncaveat and providing absolute clarity regarding the lawful development of the property.\nWe trust this clarifies the nature and intent of this retrospective application.\n",
